24. Performance Tips ⚡

For normal lists:

products.map(...)

is perfectly fine.

But very large lists can contain thousands of elements.

For example:

10 items       → easy
100 items      → easy
1,000 items    → usually manageable
100,000 items  → potentially expensive

Large lists may require techniques such as:

Pagination
Virtualization
Memoization where appropriate
Server-side filtering
Search
Lazy loading

Don't prematurely optimize small lists.

25. Industry Tips 💼

In professional React applications, you'll frequently see:

data.map((item) => (
  <Component key={item.id} {...item} />
))

For example:

products.map((product) => (
  <ProductCard
    key={product.id}
    product={product}
  />
))

This is a cleaner architecture.

Instead of making App responsible for displaying every detail:

App
 │
 ├── ProductCard
 ├── ProductCard
 ├── ProductCard
 └── ProductCard

Each ProductCard handles its own UI.

We'll build toward this pattern as you progress.

